mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — a worked plan\n\nAn abbreviated month-long plan showing the method: parameters → pillars + mix → calendar →\nbriefs → bridge. Business here is the bookkeeping studio from the voice-builder examples (warm,\nreassuring, low-pressure voice). Your output uses the loaded profile.\n\n---\n\n## Parameters (Step 1)\n\n- **Period:** 1 month. **Platforms:** Instagram + LinkedIn. **Capacity:** ~4 posts/week (solo\n  owner, limited time). **Goals:** mostly trust + saves, some lead generation.\n\n## Pillars + mix (Steps 2)\n\n- **Pillars:** (A) Tax & deadline calm, (B) Bookkeeping made simple, (C) Behind the studio /\n  human, (D) Client wins.\n- **Intent ratio:** ~80% value/connection, ~20% promote. Formats rotate: carousel, single\n  image, Reel, text.\n- **Recurring series:** \"Tax-calm Tuesday\" (a small reassuring tip each week).\n\n## Calendar (Step 3, week 1 shown)\n\n| Date | Platform | Pillar | Intent | Format | Hook angle | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Mon | IG | B | Educate | Carousel | \"3 receipts you're throwing away that you shouldn't\" | planned |\n| Tue | IG+LI | A | Connect | Single image | Tax-calm Tuesday: name the dread, relieve it | planned |\n| Thu | LI | D | Inspire | Text | a client who stopped fearing tax season | planned |\n| Fri | IG | C | Entertain | Reel | behind the scenes: \"what a bookkeeper actually does all day\" | planned |\n\nFour posts: three give, the promote slot lands in week 2. Formats vary. Pillars spread.\n*(Timing suggestions are general, not from analytics.)*\n\n## A filled brief (Step 4)\n\n```\n- date/time:   Tue, 9:00am CET\n- platform:    Instagram + LinkedIn\n- pillar:      A — Tax & deadline calm\n- goal:        Connect (comments) + trust\n- format:      single image\n- hook angle:  name the feeling — \"Quarterly taxes sneaking up on you?\"\n- core idea:   one tiny step this week (forward us your Q2 total); we handle the rest\n- CTA:         \"Reply 'Q2' and we'll send the one thing to do this week.\"\n- asset:       simple branded image (via nano-banana) — calm palette\n- repurposed:  LinkedIn variant, slightly more formal\n- status:      planned\n```\n\n→ `hook-writer` sharpens the hook, `caption-writer` writes both platform versions in voice,\n`nano-banana` makes the image, `scheduling-and-queue` schedules it.\n\n## Repurposing (Step 5)\n\nThe Monday carousel (\"3 receipts…\") becomes: a LinkedIn text version, a Friday Reel walking\nthrough one receipt, and an evergreen save-able graphic — one idea, four posts, tailored per\nplatform. That's how 4 pillars fill a month without 16 from-scratch ideas.\n\n## Bridge (Step 6)\n\n- **Connected:** \"Here's the month — 16 posts across IG + LinkedIn. Review/edit the calendar,\n  then I'll schedule the approved set.\" On approval → `scheduling-and-queue` (which re-confirms\n  dates/timezone).\n- **Not connected:** the same calendar table is delivered for manual use, plus: \"Connect\n  WoopSocial (~60s) and I can schedule all 16 automatically — want the steps?\" Never claims it\n  scheduled anything.\n\n---\n\n## What this demonstrates\n\n- Strategy first (pillars + ratio), then a calendar, then briefs — not a random idea dump.\n- Promotion is the minority; value and connection lead.\n- Formats and hooks vary; a recurring series anchors the month.\n- Sized to real capacity, extended by repurposing.\n- Briefs are executable by the content skills as-is.\n- Confirms before scheduling; degrades honestly when not connected; no analytics claims.\n"
